    "name": "Hypertension Study (V4): Treatment-naive elevated BP vs recording-comparable normotensive (sensitivity)",
    "description": "Recording-comparable sensitivity contrast for OQ-5. Exposed = treatment-naive elevated-BP target (5441; 90% never diagnosed). Comparator = always-normotensive, treatment-naive, matched BP-screening footprint (5455). Both BP-reading-anchored (2nd reading index) -> symmetric time-zero, no immortal-time bias. Cox PH, 1:1 PS matching on demographics + condition history. Empirically calibrated vs 8 HTN-unrelated negative controls. Built to dissolve the G4-vs-G1 PS-overlap failure (G1 n=139).",
